{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Command the children of Israel, etc.</b> This passage was said on the day the Mishkan was set up, and eight passages were said on that day, as is in tractate Gittin, chapter HaNizzakin (Gittin 60a)." "<b>They shall send outside the camp.</b> Three camps were there at the time of their encampment: inside the curtains is the camp of the Shekhinah; the encampment of the Levites around, as is explained in the passage BaMidbar Sinai, is the camp of Leviyah; and from there to the end of the camp of the standards in all four directions is the camp of Israel. The metzora is sent outside all of them. The zav is permitted in the camp of Israel and is sent from the other two. And one impure through a corpse is permitted even in that of Leviyah, and is sent only from that of the Shekhinah. And all this our Sages derived from the verses in tractate Pesachim (67a-68a)." "<b>Impure through a corpse.</b> ״דִּמְסָאָב לִטְמֵי נַפְשָׁא דֶאֱנָשָׁא״ — I say that this is a term for human bones in Aramaic. And there are many in the Targum: ״אַדְרִיאָנוּס שְׁחִיק טַמְיָא״ — שְׁחִיק is bones."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:09:29.014132030Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}